    {
      "id": "serialize-with-object",
      "name": "SerializeWithObject",
      "category": "ReliableNetBlobQueue",
      "signature": "SerializeWithObject(Target, Context, Ref Handle, Out Record)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FReliableNetBlobQueue*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Context",
          "type": "FNetSerializationContext&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Ref Handle",
          "type": "FNetRefHandle"
        },
        {
          "name": "Out Record",
          "type": "FReplicationRecord&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "UInt",
      "docs": "Serializes as many blobs as possible using their respective SerializeWithObject() method. It is assumed the NetRefHandle will be\nreconstructed somehow on the receiving end and passed to DeserializeWithObject().\nThis provides an opportunity for FNetObjectAttachments, such as FNetRPCs, to avoid serializing the same NetRefHandle redundantly.\n@param Context A FNetSerializationContext.\n@param RefHandle The handle for the blobs' target object.\n@param OutRecord The record to pass to CommitReplicationRecord() if a packet containing the serialized data was sent.\n@return The number of blobs that were serialized."
    },
